# The Codexify-side host-owned job attribution, as proposed.
#
# PR #1027 (fix(music): the host owns the job's attribution), opened
# 2026-11-07. The branch carries the code change, its migration, the
# dated receipt, the qualification-registry regeneration the change
# requires, and a dated note on ADR-108.
#
# Apply onto cbc5dee70, or onto any later commit that has not changed
# guardian/routes/music_projects.py, guardian/core/pgdb.py,
# guardian/db/models.py, guardian/db/migrations/versions/**,
# docs/architecture/00-current-state.md, docs/architecture/README.md,
# docs/architecture/adr/108-... or docs/qualification/registry.json.
#
# The route read which project a finished music job belongs to out of the
# context the service echoed back on the job. That made the host's
# attribution depend on the engine's age: an engine that does not echo
# the context -- v0.1.2, which discards it at the source -- returns
# files the host cannot place, and the host reports success anyway.
# Files produced, none registered. The same silent failure PR #1003
# fixed, one layer up.
#
# The host sent the context, so it now keeps its own copy, in a new
# music_jobs table, written when the job handle is minted. The first
# write wins. At poll time the host's record is the answer and the
# service's echo is the logged fallback. A refused write does not fail
# the compose.
#
# docs/qualification/registry.json is in this patch because
# guardian/routes/**, guardian/core/**, guardian/db/models.py and
# guardian/db/migrations/** are all inside qualified surfaces. The
# registry has to be regenerated in the same change or it states
# something untrue. Generate it with full repository history: a shallow
# clone resolves the qualification run's tested commit as outside the
# tip's lineage and emits a different, false registry.
#
# The registry is carried here as text. docs/qualification/*.json is
# marked -diff in .gitattributes, so a plain `git diff` renders it
# binary; `git diff --text` is what produces this patch.
#
diff --git a/docs/architecture/00-current-state.md b/docs/architecture/00-current-state.md
